# ModSettingsTool-IL2CPP — Cursor / agent rules

## Context tiers

- **Auto-read:** `AGENTS.md` and `.claude/skills/ARCHITECTURE_INVARIANTS.md`.
- **On demand:** `CLAUDE.md` (authoritative manifest — wins on conflict), plus `docs/*` per CLAUDE.md § Conditional reads.
- OpenCode setup: `docs/OPENCODE.md`. MCP parameter names: `docs/AGENT-TOOLS.md`.

## OpenCode MCP (Cursor bridge)

When this workspace is driven through OpenCode (`@openchamber/opencode-cursor`), use **only** OpenCode MCP tools (`read`, `grep`, `glob`, `bash`, `write`, `edit`, `skill`, `opencode_task`) — not native Cursor file/shell tools. `read` uses `filePath` (not `path`). Project root is the shell cwd (worktrees included).

## Policy

- Never trigger Codex, `@codex review`, or other bot/cloud reviews unless the owner explicitly asked in this session.
- Do not commit, push, merge, or publish unless the owner asked.

